#X obj 660 11 color.scale;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 297 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object builds a color scale from a list of reference
colors and outputs a color at a given position on that scale. The position
is set with a float on the inlet: 0 corresponds to the first color
in the list \, 1 to the last color \, and values in between give a
smooth transition. The interpolation strategy is controlled by the
@interp property.;
#X text 240 199 Interpolation is performed by the colorm library. The
@interp property selects the hue interpolation strategy and accepts
the following values: 'none' — colors are interpolated directly in
RGB \, no hue correction is applied \, 'short' — interpolation goes
along the shorter arc of the hue circle (default for most cases) \,
'long' — interpolation goes along the longer arc of the hue circle
\, 'inc' — hue increases monotonically (clockwise on the hue circle)
\, 'dec' — hue decreases monotonically (counter-clockwise on the hue
circle).;
